# Security Rules

- Hash passwords using Argon2id or an equivalently strong password hashing algorithm.
- Hash the ward code separately from user passwords.
- Use secure, HTTP only cookies for browser sessions.
- Use short lived access tokens and secure refresh handling for mobile.
- Add rate limiting to authentication.
- Record failed login attempts without storing attempted passwords.
- Store external provider secrets in a managed secret store in production.
- Encrypt sensitive values at rest where appropriate.
- Apply server side role and permission checks to every protected route.
- Minimize access to date of birth and minor contact information.
- Audit exports and bulk access.
- Redact personal data from logs.
- Validate and normalize email addresses and phone numbers.
- Never send contact data to AI providers unless explicitly required and approved.
- Include data retention and deletion hooks in the design.
